Subject: [PATCH 11/12] feat: `brit merge-base --is-ancestor` answering through
 its exit code

Requested by the integrating session (68 uses in the agents' fallback
census, all reading the exit code). Added to Brit's existing `merge-base`
verb: one field on its clap struct, one branch in its dispatch arm, and
`is_ancestor` beside `merge_base` in gitoxide-core.

Like Git: 0 when the first commit is an ancestor of the second or the
same commit, 1 when it is not, 128 with `fatal: Not a valid object name`
or `Not a valid commit name` for a bad revision, 128 for more than two
commits, and the usage status 129 for one. Nothing is printed on stdout.
The oracle journey compares stdout, status and stderr emptiness with Git.

